%% The two request paths that carry the system: storing an assessment, and
%% reading the report it produced. Refusals are shown where they arise, since
%% where a request is refused is what a client has to account for.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Client
    participant M as Middleware
    participant H as Handler
    participant P as Lockfile parser
    participant D as PostgreSQL

    Note over C,D: Submission

    C->>M: POST /api/v1/assessments
    M->>M: Assign x-request-id, open a span, arm the timeout
    M->>H: Request, with the body unread
    H->>H: Read the body up to the configured length
    alt Longer than the deployment accepts
        H--)C: 413 manifest-too-large
    end
    H->>P: Lockfile text, or an entry list as JSON
    alt Not parsable
        P-->>H: Failure, with the line where known
        H--)C: 422 manifest-unreadable
    end
    P-->>H: Entries, depth from a breadth-first walk
    alt More entries than the deployment accepts
        H--)C: 413 manifest-too-large
    end
    H->>H: Mint 32 random bytes as the report token
    H->>D: create_report, definer rights, one transaction
    alt No completed ingestion run, or no current model
        D-->>H: object_not_in_prerequisite_state
        H--)C: 503 not-ready
    end
    D-->>H: Report stored, manifest fingerprint kept
    H->>D: Read the report and its ranked entries
    D-->>H: Header and entries
    H-->>C: 201, Location, the report and the link, issued once

    Note over C,D: Retrieval

    C->>M: GET /api/v1/reports/{token}
    M->>H: Request
    H->>D: Report header, addressed by the digest of the token
    alt No such row
        H--)C: 404 report-not-found
    else Withdrawn
        H--)C: 410 report-withdrawn, with the reason
    end
    D-->>H: Header as stored
    H->>D: Entries, in their stored rank
    D-->>H: Entries
    H-->>C: 200, the report as it stood when generated
